        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-28T13:12:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m itching to use string_view more, but I\u0027m not convinced it\u0027s right here. string_view doesn\u0027t implement c_str(), because in general it\u0027s not guaranteed to be null-terminated.\nAnd pretty much all I do with these is pass them to open() which just wants a pointer to a null-terminated string (and doesn\u0027t care about the length).",
      "parentUuid": "f81c5b61_7f4e7efa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 71,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 71,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "3d5cc3451abf1fab09fcdebe4aa9695018a47500",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
